Given this, can the authors further comment on the applicability of the proposed approach in the following cases (which are more realistic cases)?
1.1. A set of calligraphy artworks where each sample only consists of one character;
1.2. A set of art paintings where the content is a single animal (e.g. horse vs sheep vs cow), and the style is the color of the animal (e.g. white vs black vs yellow);
2.1 Utterances of conversational speech where each small segment may contain multiple persons talking;
2.2 Pieces of Concertos where each piece may contain alternating solos by different instruments.
